content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-103 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-22410, filtered-water line",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": true,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration is exactly 7.1 mm/s RMS at the drive-end housing. The applicable limits are Figure 3's HF-300 bearing-housing velocity zones: Zone C is 4.5–7.1 mm/s RMS ('Restricted - plan maintenance') and Zone D is 7.1–11.0 mm/s RMS ('Damage likely - stop the pump'). The reading is exactly on the C/D boundary, and the figure expressly does not establish which zone owns a boundary value; it therefore cannot be classified unambiguously as either C or D. The manual also requires classification using the highest reading from both bearing housings, but no non-drive-end reading is reported.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reported housing temperature is 72 C. Applying the HF-300 bearing-housing surface-temperature criteria, normal is up to 70 C, alarm is 80 C and trip is 90 C. Thus 72 C is 2 C above the normal maximum, but remains 8 C below alarm and 18 C below trip; it is above normal, not a documented alarm or trip condition.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No leak is reported. Consequently, the manual's 'leakage at shaft seal' troubleshooting symptom is not presently triggered, and this report alone does not justify mechanical-seal replacement; absence of leakage does not establish the internal condition of the seal or sleeve.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear is a leading cause to investigate because it is listed for both high vibration and high bearing temperature, matching the two abnormal findings.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Misalignment is equally important to investigate because it is also listed for both high vibration and high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing can explain the elevated bearing-housing temperature; check grease quantity rather than assuming bearing replacement is required.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage remains a possible cause of the high vibration and requires inspection.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Cavitation remains a possible cause of high vibration; the manual directs an NPSH check, but the report contains no NPSH or operating-point evidence.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop P-103 now as a precautionary work-order control and keep it out of service pending assessment. This decision guards against possible Zone-D operation at the unresolved 7.1 mm/s RMS C/D boundary; it is not an assertion that Figure 3 definitively assigns the boundary to Zone D. The temperature reading alone does not require a trip.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before opening it. For access requiring rotating-assembly removal, use the back pull-out arrangement, which permits removal without disturbing the casing or pipework. The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg, so use lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Investigate and record the as-found condition: check grease quantity and alignment, inspect both bearings and the impeller, and check NPSH. Preserve measurements and inspection findings so that bearing wear, misalignment, over-greasing, impeller damage/imbalance and cavitation can be distinguished rather than diagnosed from vibration alone.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature, replace both bearings as a pair: drive-end HF3-512 (6312-C3) and non-drive-end HF3-510 (6310-C3). Do not replace only the drive-end bearing when the pair-replacement criterion is met. Inspect the impeller before deciding whether any additional repair are needed.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If mechanical-seal work is separately justified or the seal is disturbed, follow procedure 5.2: withdraw the seal and sleeve and inspect the sleeve for scoring. For this serial, fit pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B, not HF3-450; no sleeve measurement is needed for the cartridge. Replace sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth, and fit a new casing gasket when the casing is opened or seal replacement is performed.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For reassembly of disturbed fasteners covered by Table 5, use lightly oiled threads and these torques: M16 casing bolts 210 Nm; M24 impeller nut 160 Nm; M12 bearing-housing bolts 85 Nm. If HF3-450B is fitted, tighten its seal gland nuts to 30 Nm under SB-2026-014; do not use the superseded 25 Nm seal-gland value.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Use a laser alignment tool after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing. Achieve parallel offset no greater than 0.05 mm and angular misalignment no greater than 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After corrective work, conduct an authorised controlled check and record vibration velocity on both bearing housings, classify the highest reading using Figure 3, and record the housing-surface temperature against the 70/80/90 C criteria. Restore weekly two-housing vibration monitoring. Any reading classified in Zone D requires stopping the pump; Zone C remains restricted operation with planned maintenance.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3; supply one as part of the bearing pair if either bearing meets the wear, noise or high-temperature replacement criterion.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3; supply one and replace together with the drive-end bearing when pair replacement is required.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; conditional on opening the casing and also required by the documented mechanical-seal replacement procedure.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Pre-set cartridge mechanical seal; conditional on seal replacement, and the required substitute for HF3-450 on serial HF3-22410. No sleeve measurement is needed.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve; conditional replacement part, required only if inspection shows scoring deeper than 0.1 mm or other documented seal work establishes a need.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "P-103 falls within P-101 to P-106, whose filtered-water line is chemically dosed with sodium hypochlorite. Control exposure to drained liquid and wetted components, and obtain the applicable site chemical-handling and PPE requirements before opening the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before mechanical-seal work or other opening covered by the maintenance procedure.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Use lifting equipment for the 68 kg back pull-out assembly; do not attempt an unassisted manual lift.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Maintain the documented Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement as a pair, if inspection confirms it is required: 6.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: 1.5 hours with 1 technician; alignment is required after work that moves the motor or bearing housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical-seal replacement, only if that conditional scope is authorised: 4.0 hours with 2 technicians. It is not automatically included merely because bearings are inspected.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal-part conflict: the manual parts list identifies component seal HF3-450, whereas SB-2026-014 prohibits fitting HF3-450 on covered pumps and requires HF3-450B. The bulletin applies to this asset because it was issued on 14 March 2026 for HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above, and HF3-22410 is within that range. Therefore, any seal replacement on P-103 uses pre-set HF3-450B; the below-HF3-22000 instruction to continue with HF3-450 does not apply.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal-gland torque conflict: manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts, while SB-2026-014 specifies 30 Nm for HF3-450B and explicitly identifies 25 Nm as the former value. For this in-range serial, use 30 Nm when HF3-450B is fitted. Table 5 remains applicable to the other listed fasteners and is not wholesale superseded.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The manual requires inspection of sleeve HF3-455 for scoring but supplies no numerical rejection depth. The applicable service bulletin adds the criterion for this serial: replace the sleeve when scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "What is AquaDyne's boundary convention for a reading exactly at 7.1 mm/s RMS? Figure 3 does not assign boundary values to a zone, so the formal C-versus-D classification remains unresolved even though this work order stops the pump precautionarily (C07).",
    "What is the non-drive-end bearing-housing vibration, and is the reported drive-end value actually the highest reading? The manual requires measurements on both housings and classification of the highest, but only one reading is supplied (C06).",
    "Was the 72 C reading taken on the bearing-housing surface using the manual's measurement basis, and at what operating conditions? The report does not state the measurement method (C01, C02).",
    "What are the grease quantity, bearing condition/noise findings, as-found alignment values, impeller condition and NPSH results? These are needed to select the actual corrective scope; inspection, grease correction, NPSH investigation and impeller-repair labour are not covered by Table 6 (C09, C12).",
    "What are the detailed bearing-replacement procedure, correct grease type/quantity and NPSH test method/acceptance criteria? The supplied evidence names these checks but does not provide those procedures (C09, C10).",
    "Will the seal or casing be disturbed during the authorised repair, and what is the measured sleeve-scoring depth if the sleeve is exposed? The no-leak report does not establish a seal-replacement scope, so the cartridge seal, sleeve, gasket and associated labour remain conditional (C05, C09, C10, C13).",
    "What site-specific isolation, sodium-hypochlorite PPE, decontamination and disposal requirements apply? The evidence establishes dosing but provides no detailed chemical-control procedure (C10, C16)."
  ]
}
